msgstr ""

#: ../../doc_src/interactive.rst:235
msgid ""
"When it is fish's turn to ask for input (like after it started or the "
"command ended), it will show a prompt. Often this looks something like::"
msgstr ""

#: ../../doc_src/interactive.rst:239
msgid ""
"This prompt is determined by running the :doc:`fish_prompt "
"<cmds/fish_prompt>` and :doc:`fish_right_prompt <cmds/fish_right_prompt>`"
" functions."
msgstr ""

#: ../../doc_src/interactive.rst:241
msgid ""
"The output of the former is displayed on the left and the latter's output"
" on the right side of the terminal. For :ref:`vi mode <vi-mode>`, the "
"output of :doc:`fish_mode_prompt <cmds/fish_mode_prompt>` will be "
"prepended on the left."
