#: ../../doc_src/interactive.rst:280
msgid ""
"The :doc:`status current-command <cmds/status>` builtin will always "
"return the name of the job to be put into the foreground (or ``fish`` if "
"control is returning to the shell) when the :doc:`fish_title "
"<cmds/fish_title>` function is called. The first argument will contain "
"the most recently executed foreground command as a string."
msgstr ""

#: ../../doc_src/interactive.rst:282
msgid ""
"The default title shows the hostname if connected via ssh, the currently "
"running command (unless it is fish) and the current working directory. "
"All of this is shortened to not make the tab too wide."
msgstr ""

